# Aug 17, 2026, approved by Indy in session. `.oracle/ruleset.lock` was the
# rule-content ledger: a map of rule path → SHA-256 digest of that rule's bytes.
# `generic-api-key` matches on entropy alone, so a hex digest reads to it
# exactly like a credential. Both hits are digests, not secrets.
#
# These surfaced only once `.gitleaks.toml` was deleted. That file held nothing
# but an `[allowlist]`, and a local config REPLACES the default ruleset unless
# it carries `[extend] useDefault = true` — so gitleaks had been loading zero
# rules and calling every scan clean. If you add a config back, extend the
# defaults; do not replace them.
